{#
  The Race Overview, Markdown family. One Race's whole catalogue as four flat,
  cross-linked sections — Units, Models, Equipment, Spawns — followed by the
  Rules Reference (ADR 0031). A fielded Army has one chosen path through Unit,
  Model and Equipment, which is why the Army Reference nests them; a Race is an
  N:M web, so every record prints exactly once here and the links carry the
  structure instead.

  Each section opens with a summary table whose first cell links into the
  record's own entry below it. The gist columns are mechanical — a size, a slot
  table, a range profile — never prose.

  Every block below emits a leading newline and none emits a trailing one, so a
  block that renders to nothing leaves no blank line behind. That is the same
  `{%- if -%}` idiom the Army Reference body is written in.

  The explicit `<a id>` is required, not decorative: `md_to_html` generates no
  heading ids, so without it every cross-link breaks in the derived HTML. Raw
  HTML passes through CommonMark untouched and is harmless in a plain `.md`.

  Section headings anchor under `section-`, a fifth namespace disjoint both from
  the four a record carries and from the Rules Reference's `rule-`.
#}
{%- macro links(items) -%}
{% for link in items %}{% if not loop.first %}, {% endif %}[{{ link.name }}](#{{ link.anchor }}){% endfor %}
{%- endmacro -%}

{#- A rule's name, linked when the Rules Reference holds its entry. -#}
{%- macro rule(line) -%}
{% if line.anchor %}[{{ line.name }}](#{{ line.anchor }}){% else %}{{ line.name }}{% endif %}
{%- endmacro -%}

{%- macro bullets(lines) -%}
{% for line in lines %}
- **{{ rule(line) }}**{% if line.text %}: {{ line.text }}{% endif %}
{%- endfor %}
{%- endmacro -%}

{#- One Slot's Specials, under the label naming what the Slot grants. Slots
    stay apart: what a record grants its Unit and what it is itself are
    different claims. -#}
{%- macro slot_specials(label, lines) -%}
{% if lines %}
- *{{ label }}:*
{%- for line in lines %}
    - **{{ rule(line) }}**{% if line.text %}: {{ line.text }}{% endif %}
{%- endfor %}
{%- endif %}
{%- endmacro -%}

{#- Declared deltas: a Stacker is printed as the change it declares, never
    resolved, because it has no value until a Unit is fielded under it. -#}
{%- macro deltas(label, modifiers) -%}
{% if modifiers %}
- *{{ label }}:*
{%- for modifier in modifiers %}
    - {{ modifier }}
{%- endfor %}
{%- endif %}
{%- endmacro -%}

{%- macro order_table(title, rows) -%}
{%- set ncols = (rows | map('last') | map('length') | list | max) if rows else 1 %}

**{{ title }}**

| Speed |{{ ' |' * ncols }}
|{{ ' --- |' * (ncols + 1) }}
{%- for speed, cells in rows %}
| {{ speed }} |{% for cell in cells %} {{ cell }} |{% endfor %}{{ ' |' * (ncols - cells | length) }}
{%- endfor %}
{%- endmacro -%}

{#- The cost cells of a summary row, one column per currency. -#}
{%- macro cost_cells(columns) -%}
{% for cell in columns %} {{ cell }} |{% endfor %}
{%- endmacro -%}
# {{ source.title }}

*v{{ spf_version }}*
{%- if source.description %}

{{ source.description | trim }}
{%- endif %}
{%- if source.race_image %}

![{{ source.race }}]({{ source.race_image | relative_to(output_dir) }})
{%- endif %}

## Contents

- [Units](#section-units)
- [Models](#section-models)
- [Equipment](#section-equipment)
{%- if source.spawns %}
- [Spawns](#section-spawns)
{%- endif %}
{%- if source.rules and source.rules.entries %}
- [{{ source.rules.title }}](#section-rules)
{%- endif %}

<a id="section-units"></a>

## Units

| Unit | Size | Models | ip | mp | xp | cp | vpm |
| --- | --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |
{%- for unit in source.units %}
| [{{ unit.name }}](#{{ unit.anchor }}) | {{ unit.size }} | {{ unit.model_count }} |{{ cost_cells(unit.cost_columns) }}
{%- endfor %}
{% for unit in source.units %}
<a id="{{ unit.anchor }}"></a>

### {{ unit.name }}
{%- if unit.lore %}

*{{ unit.lore | trim }}*
{%- endif %}
{%- if unit.image %}

![{{ unit.name }}]({{ unit.image | relative_to(output_dir) }})
{%- endif %}
{#- The one undashed `if` of an entry: the newline its own line contributes is
    what opens the blank line under the heading, whether or not the field
    below is there to print. #}
{% if unit.cost %}
- Cost: {{ unit.cost }} ({{ unit.points }} points)
{%- endif %}
- Size: {{ unit.size }}
- Models: {{ links(unit.models) }}
{%- if unit.types %}
- Type: {{ unit.types | join(', ') }}
{%- endif %}
{%- if unit.armor %}
- Armor: {{ unit.armor | join('/') }}
{%- endif %}
- Shaken: {{ unit.shaken_speed }} [{{ unit.shaken_movement | join(', ') }}] / {{ unit.shaken_fire }}
{%- if unit.spawned_by %}
- Placed by: {{ links(unit.spawned_by) }}
{%- endif %}
{{- bullets(unit.specials) }}
{%- if unit.spawn_links %}
- Places: {{ links(unit.spawn_links) }}
{%- endif %}
{%- if unit.note %}
- **Note**: {{ unit.note | trim }}
{%- endif %}
{#- The tip is army-building advice and may run to several paragraphs, so it
    is a block of its own rather than a bullet a second paragraph would break
    out of. -#}
{%- if unit.tip %}

**Tip**: {{ unit.tip | trim }}
{%- endif %}
{{- order_table("Movement orders", unit.movement_rows) }}
{{- order_table("Fire orders", unit.fire_rows) }}
{%- for name, rows, notes in unit.damage_tables %}

**Damage Table: {{ name }}**

| Roll | Effect |
| ---- | ------ |
{%- for roll, effect in rows %}
| {{ roll }} | {{ effect }} |
{%- endfor %}
{%- if notes %}
{% for note in notes %}
- {{ note }}
{%- endfor %}
{%- endif %}
{%- endfor %}
{% endfor %}
